[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/dialogue/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n4_simon"
text = "# DRAFT
# Brother Simon at dusk, in the cloister garth on the low wall of the herb beds (night 4, fog). A quiet choir brother; nervous.
# Not in the cult. Thomas has sent him to do a dirty job tonight (scrubbing blood) and he can't say so.
# If Thomas has named him (n4_thomas_simon), the porter can ask where he goes at night (trust -5: he takes it badly).
# Telling him to keep to the dormitory is a warning ([warn]); he takes it badly, and he trusts Thomas more than the porter.
== start
(A thin brother on the wall of the herb beds, picking at a thread on his sleeve. He stands too fast when he sees you.)
Simon: Porter. I was only taking the air. There's not much else to take tonight.
-> topics

== again
(Simon is back on the wall, picking at the same thread.)
Simon: Porter.
-> topics

== topics
* [if n4_thomas_simon] [if not n4_simon_night] (Ask where he goes at night.) -> night
* [if not n4_simon_how] (Ask how he's keeping.) -> how
* [if not n4_simon_warn] (Tell him to keep to the dormitory tonight.) [warn] -> warn

== night [set n4_simon_night] [trust simon -5]
(The thread snaps in his fingers.)
Simon: Who says I go anywhere? I can't sleep. I walk. Is that a sin now, with all the rest?
(He looks toward the infirmary, then at the ground.)
-> topics

== how [set n4_simon_how]
Simon: Hungry. Cold. Afraid, like everyone.
Simon: I came here to sing, porter. It's all I'm good for. I wish they'd let me only sing.
-> topics

== warn [set n4_simon_warn]
(He goes white.)
Simon: Why would you say that to me? Who told you to say it?
Simon: I'll go where I'm bid. I'm a brother of this house, not a guest you can lock in.
Simon: Don't tell anyone you said that to me. Please.
-> end

== leave
Simon: God keep you, porter.
"
